<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115735" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῑλο-κῐθᾰριστής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιλὸς κιθαριστής</span>
			 (which is found in <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
				66
			</span></i> (pl.)), <i>one who plays the</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιθάρα</span>”
				<i>without singing to it, instrumental performer,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chares
					4J.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				10.452f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suet.
				<u>Dom.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῑλο-κῐθᾰρεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				2759
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Aphrodisias</span>):—and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψῑλο-κῐθᾰριστική</span></b>  (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) ἡ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιλὴ κιθάρισις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philoch.
			</span></i> l. c.:—cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψιλός</span>
				IV.<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
